> Iam porting a c application code  source files from tru64 os on alpha
> to ia64 on debian linux kernel 2.6 iam getting the following errors
> will u kindly help me in this regard
>
> scn_buffer.c:52: warning: cast to pointer from integer of different
> size
> scn_buffer.c:57: warning: cast to pointer from integer of different
> size
>
> uabgembt@112-27A:~/kant/kant1/kant2$ gcc -c scn_timer.c
> scn_timer.c: In function `tm_start':
> scn_timer.c:193: warning: cast to pointer from integer of different
> size

Those warnings mean you are doing something like

  int i = 0;
  void *p = (void *) i;

and sizeof(int) != sizeof(void *).

Are you seeing these warnings on ia64 but not on Alpha?  Then you are
probably casting a long to a pointer.  On Alpha, long is 64 bits, as
well as pointers.  It could be that your compiler uses 32-bit longs on
ia64, I don't have one of those, so I don't know.  If this is the
case, change the offending long variables to long long, which should
be 64 bits.

